=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The reported symptom — Office department hosts (192.168.3.x) unable to reach
the Server Room and Internet Lab — does not exist in the live lab at the time
of investigation. Exhaustive probing across all campus segments showed zero
packet loss on every tested path.

All three routers are running RIPv2 correctly. Router1 (the Office gateway,
192.168.3.1) holds RIP-learned routes to 1.0.0.0/8 (Server Room, via
router2) and 128.168.0.0/16 (Internet Lab, via router2), as well as to
192.168.1.0/24 and 192.168.2.0/24 (IT and CS Labs, via router0). Router2
and router0 both carry return routes to 192.168.3.0/24. No iptables firewall
rules are installed on any router. All LAN and WAN interfaces are up and
correctly addressed. Office hosts (office_pc, enquiry, exam_cell, tpo) all
have valid 192.168.3.x addresses and a correct default gateway pointing to
router1.

Direct ICMP tests from multiple office machines to every remote segment —
Server Room (pc1 at 1.0.0.5), Internet Lab (pc2/pc3 at 128.168.0.x), IT Lab
(192.168.1.x), and CS Lab (192.168.2.x) — all completed with 0 % packet
loss and normal round-trip times (~1–3 ms).

Root cause: The network is fully operational; the helpdesk ticket describes a
connectivity loss that is not present in the infrastructure.

Corrective action: No network change is required. The issue should be
investigated on the end-user side (e.g., a transient host-level problem that
self-resolved, a misidentified destination address, or a temporary local
ARP/DNS issue on the reporting machine at the time of the complaint).
=== END ===
```